From b4e32bebd184b96bc9a7784ca50d5631c7e4661c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:02:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 189/191] IOP interpreter: one instruction read, RAM accesses
 inline, no calls for work that is not there

Per interpreted instruction the emulator read the instruction twice through an out-of-line IopMemory::read32 that
tests three device ranges before RAM (once for the import-stub check, once to execute), called takeDmaStart (an
optional copied and reset), synchronizeSpu and the PC sampler. Same results, less work:

- IopMemory::read8/16/32 and write8/16/32 answer RAM inline; the general functions (now *Slow) take the rest. No
  device range lies inside RAM, so asking for RAM first cannot change an answer.
- step() reads the instruction once and passes it to IopCpuCore::executeInstruction(cpu, instruction); the import
  registry is asked only for `jr ra`, the first word of every import stub.
- schedulePendingDma returns at once unless a register write started a DMA (IopMemory::hasDmaStart).
- synchronizeSpu's between-samples test is inline, the rest out of line; the PC sampler's switch is read once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
